[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4428618150","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13916#issuecomment-4428618150","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13916","id":4428618150,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM8AAAABB_dZpg","user":{"login":"andruud","id":77163,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MTYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77163?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud","html_url":"https://github.com/andruud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-12T08:18:02Z","updated_at":"2026-05-12T08:18:02Z","body":"> change the spec for `revert` so that it explicitly only can find weaker rules\n\nThis is my preference. I also suspect that `revert` being capable of \"reverting\" to something _stronger_ wasn't very intentional in the first place.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4428618150/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4433874264","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13916#issuecomment-4433874264","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13916","id":4433874264,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM8AAAABCEeNWA","user":{"login":"Loirooriol","id":7477678,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0Nzc2Nzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7477678?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loirooriol","html_url":"https://github.com/Loirooriol","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loirooriol/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loirooriol/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loirooriol/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loirooriol/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loirooriol/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loirooriol/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loirooriol/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loirooriol/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Loirooriol/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-12T19:12:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-12T19:12:17Z","body":"I think the problem is with `revert-rule`, not `revert`. Instead of\n\n> the cascaded value is rolled back such that the [specified value](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-5/#specified-value) is calculated as if the current [style rule](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-syntax-3/#style-rule) had not been present at all\n\nI think it should rather behave exactly as `revert-layer` would, if each rule was wrapped inside a sublayer.\n\nE.g. here `revert-layer` has a different behavior than removing the layer:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<style>\n#foo {\n  @layer { color: magenta }\n  @layer { color: revert-layer !important; }\n  @layer { color: cyan; }\n}\n#bar {\n  @layer { color: magenta }\n/*@layer { color: revert-layer !important; }*/\n  @layer { color: cyan; }\n}\n</style>\n<div id=\"foo\">magenta</div>\n<div id=\"bar\">cyan</div>\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4433874264/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4438630108","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13916#issuecomment-4438630108","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13916","id":4438630108,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM8AAAABCJAe3A","user":{"login":"andruud","id":77163,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MTYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77163?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud","html_url":"https://github.com/andruud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andruud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T07:51:01Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T07:51:01Z","body":"I see how that would be consistent, but it would mean that e.g. `if(style(--toggle): green; else: revert-rule)`[^1] would not really work anymore as an `!important` declaration. I think that's a net loss.\n\n[^1]: \"Make this green if `--toggle`, otherwise _have no effect at all_\". ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4438630108/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]